    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm hitting a CrashLoopBackOff on a microservice in our GKE cluster and i can't figure out why. here are the logs:\n\ncontainer_log:\n{\"level\":\"error\",\"msg\":\"failed to connect to db: connection refused\",\"timestamp\":\"2023-10-27T10:15:01Z\"}\n{\"level\":\"fatal\",\"msg\":\"shutdown initiated\",\"timestamp\":\"2023-10-27T10:15:02Z\"}\n\ncan u give me a diagnostic checklist to see if this is a resource issue, a liveness probe failure, or something in the config?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The logs clearly indicate your service is failing because it cannot connect to its database, not necessarily due to resource constraints or probes. Start by verifying network connectivity between your microservice pod and the database service/pod. Next, confirm that the database service is running, accessible network-wise, and listening on the expected port specified in your microservice's configuration. Finally, double-check your environment variables or mounted secrets to ensure correct connection strings and credentials are being passed to the container.",
