    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i checked the network and the db is definitely up and reachable from other pods. the connection strings look right too. i suspect maybe it's a resource thing since it happens right at startup. how can i tell if the pod is just getting killed because it's hitting memory limits vs something actually being wrong with the app code?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To differentiate between a crash due to resource exhaustion and application logic, first check the pod events in GKE to see if `OOMKilled` (Out Of Memory Killed) is being reported. If no OOMKilled events exist, review the container's resource requests and limits in the deployment manifest, ensuring they are generous enough for startup. Additionally, try temporarily increasing the memory limit in your deployment to see if the service initializes successfully, which points to an initial resource bottleneck.",
      "source": "target",
